// Issue #52 acceptance fixture: changes the *default* container references
// at their single source of truth (`params.containers`, declared in
// conf/containers.config) and nothing else -- no module edit, no workflow
// edit, no per-process selector for the defaulted processes -- so
// tests/pipeline/adzuki_snp_pipeline.nf.test can prove the acceptance
// criterion end to end:
//
//     change conf/containers.config's value
//       -> the container each GS task actually runs in (.command.run)
//       -> the identity recorded in the GS panel manifest
//
// all three being the same string. A test that only asserted the manifest
// changed would not have proven the first arrow; a test that only asserted
// the running container changed would not have proven the second.
//
// The new default is each pinned image referenced by digest alone, its tag
// dropped (`repo:tag@sha256:x` -> `repo@sha256:x`). That is a distinct
// string from the default -- which is the whole point, since an identical
// string would prove nothing -- while naming byte-for-byte the same image
// content, so the run needs no additional image pull and never depends on a
// mutable tag still resolving to what it did when this was written. It is
// derived from the source of truth rather than written out here, so this
// fixture holds no copy of a pinned production digest and needs no edit when
// one is legitimately bumped. `includeConfig` is what makes that possible:
// `params` set by another config file is not visible while this one is
// parsed, only `params` from a file this one includes itself.
// GsContainerDefaults.digestOnly() in tests/lib/ applies the identical
// transformation so the test can state what it therefore expects to see.
includeConfig '../../../conf/containers.config'

// Deliberately placed *before* the params block below, and evaluated
// before it: this captures the original, unchanged
// conf/containers.config value for one single process, so the test can
// tell a process-specific override apart from a change to the default.
// GS_INDEX_CLASSIFIED_VARIANTS and GS_NORMALIZE_VARIANTS both run bcftools
// by default, and here they must end up on *different* containers -- this
// one pinned back to the original reference by an explicit selector, the
// other following the changed default -- which is exactly the ambiguity
// schema v1's per-tool `containers.bcftools` key could not express.
process {
    withName: '^GS_INDEX_CLASSIFIED_VARIANTS$' {
        container = params.containers.bcftools
    }
}

params {
    containers = params.containers.collectEntries { tool, reference ->
        [ tool, reference.replaceFirst(/:[^@]+@/, '@') ]
    }
}
